WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.550
Step four shows the directory-name guard.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:07.500
The fixture's rules target Azure Active
Directory, the name Learn's examples use.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.492
Ask for Microsoft Entra ID instead,
and the check stops with an

4
00:00:11.492 --> 00:00:15.562
error that names the targets the
schema does have, and exits two.

5
00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:18.159
That matters, because a wrong name would

6
00:00:18.159 --> 00:00:21.150
otherwise look like no
overlap at all, and pass.

7
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.350
Step five lists the reads
the two exports need.

8
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.321
On SailPoint, the provisioning
policy read scope,

9
00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:29.712
for the source's provisioning policies.

10
00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:32.159
On Graph, the custom security attribute

11
00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:35.274
provisioning read permission,
for the job's schema.

12
00:00:35.274 --> 00:00:39.205
Both are reads, and the writer
check itself reads files only:

13
00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:42.012
you export the two configurations by hand.

14
00:00:42.012 --> 00:00:45.294
Check your work: given two
exports and an alias list,

15
00:00:45.294 --> 00:00:48.310
you can say which attributes
have two writers.
